WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.710
This is a tree trunk.

2
00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:03.250
It's made of wood.

3
00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:04.670
This is a nail.

4
00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:06.250
It's made of steel.

5
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:10.270
Put them on giant scales, and
the tree trunk wins easily.

6
00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:13.070
So is wood heavier than steel?

7
00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:15.870
Now drop an ice cube into water.

8
00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:18.850
Ice is solid water, yet it floats.

9
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:19.670
Why?

10
00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:23.550
To find out, we need to zoom in
to the tiny particles that make

11
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:24.950
up everything.

12
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.090
In this mission, you'll see
how particles are arranged in

13
00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:33.730
solids, liquids and gases,
and meet a new idea: density.

14
00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:36.910
Your mission: find out if
wood is heavier than steel,

15
00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:39.300
and why ice floats.
